WEBVTT

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:18.351
-For Sarah?
-[man] Sarah?

00:00:18.435 --> 00:00:19.269
Yeah.

00:00:20.395 --> 00:00:23.606
["Seasons (Waiting On You)"
by Future Islands playing]

00:00:27.277 --> 00:00:28.653
[seat belt clicks]

00:00:30.739 --> 00:00:33.867
[man] Sarah's my roommate,
and she's quite the handful to live with.

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:42.751
Sarah is constantly falling
for the wrong type of guy

00:00:42.834 --> 00:00:46.129
and then thinking
that she doesn't deserve better.

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:48.798
♪ 'Cause I've been waiting on you ♪

00:00:51.342 --> 00:00:52.677
♪ Ooh-ooh, ooh-ooh ♪

00:00:52.886 --> 00:00:54.679
♪ I've been waiting on you ♪

00:00:55.138 --> 00:00:58.767
I would say that most men Sarah has dated
are unremarkable

00:00:58.850 --> 00:01:01.686
and Sarah needs to find a man
who values her.

00:01:04.314 --> 00:01:06.441
♪ As it breaks ♪

00:01:07.275 --> 00:01:08.735
♪ The summer awaits ♪

00:01:08.818 --> 00:01:11.029
[woman] I've known Sarah
for about two years.

00:01:11.112 --> 00:01:15.241
She's this perfect mix of nerdy,
but also kind of sexy and cute.

00:01:15.658 --> 00:01:18.036
She definitely talks a lot. [laughs]

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:19.871
You got to be a listener.

00:01:20.163 --> 00:01:23.041
♪ 'Cause I've been waiting on you ♪

00:01:23.166 --> 00:01:24.459
-Hey.
-Hey.

00:01:24.542 --> 00:01:26.544
-Sarah?
-Wow, hi. Are you Nick?

00:01:26.628 --> 00:01:27.921
-Yes.
-Hi.

00:01:28.004 --> 00:01:28.922
So nice to meet you.

00:01:29.005 --> 00:01:31.049
-Nice to meet you, too.
-I've heard a lot about you.

00:01:31.132 --> 00:01:32.634
Actually, I've heard nothing about you.

00:01:32.717 --> 00:01:35.762
I was about to say, "No, I've heard
nothing about you." Can I see some ID?

00:01:35.845 --> 00:01:37.388
-Yeah, let me go check real quick.
-Okay.

00:01:37.472 --> 00:01:38.973
You can't see mine just as a--

00:01:39.307 --> 00:01:41.518
-Then I'm not gonna give you mine.
-Fair. That's fair.

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:42.685
It's got to be reciprocated.

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:44.479
-[laughs] Yeah.
-Want to go inside?

00:01:44.562 --> 00:01:46.272
-Let's go inside. Yeah.
-After you.

00:01:47.315 --> 00:01:48.858
-Did you find the place all right?
-Yeah.

00:01:48.942 --> 00:01:51.319
-Good. Good.
-I know Brooklyn a little bit.

00:01:51.402 --> 00:01:53.988
-You do?
-I hang out across the street a lot, but--

00:01:54.072 --> 00:01:57.283
Oh, you do?
Do I sense a Brooklyn accent on you?

00:01:57.367 --> 00:01:58.451
No, it's Queens.

00:01:58.535 --> 00:02:00.036
-Queens!
-My father is from Brooklyn.

00:02:00.119 --> 00:02:01.204
Oh, okay.

00:02:01.412 --> 00:02:03.665
-What part of Queens?
-Bayside.

00:02:03.748 --> 00:02:05.125
-Okay.
-Are you from New York?

00:02:05.208 --> 00:02:06.876
-I am not from New York.
-I could've told.

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:08.878
-Can you guess where I'm from?
-Absolutely not.

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:10.046
You're like, "No." [laughs]

00:02:13.424 --> 00:02:14.384
So, Sarah...

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:16.219
-You're John?
-Hello. Mr. John.

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:18.680
-Hi. Mr. John?
-That's what they call me.

00:02:18.763 --> 00:02:20.181
-Mr. J--
-Yeah, it's like a nickname.

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:22.016
Nice. Okay.

00:02:22.433 --> 00:02:23.643
-[laughs]
-Are you...

00:02:23.726 --> 00:02:27.355
You're from the northeast.
I think I hear, like, a northern--

00:02:27.438 --> 00:02:30.483
-I'm from New York.
-Okay. I thought I heard a Yankee lilt.

00:02:30.567 --> 00:02:33.570
-What is a Yankee lilt?
-[mimics New York accent] Like, New York.

00:02:33.653 --> 00:02:36.406
-You're from New York.
-New York? I sound like that?

00:02:36.489 --> 00:02:38.449
-Yeah!
-I grew up in Rockaway Beach.

00:02:38.825 --> 00:02:39.909
Do you like the Ramones?

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:42.704
Yeah, of course. They have a summer house
one block away from me.

00:02:42.787 --> 00:02:44.539
-Shut the front door.
-Yeah.

00:02:44.956 --> 00:02:46.916
What the Franklin Delano? That's crazy.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:47.876
[laughs]

00:02:47.959 --> 00:02:50.670
Yeah, so, I like that one.
You mind if I use that?

00:02:51.171 --> 00:02:52.088
You can borrow it.

00:02:52.172 --> 00:02:53.506
[laughs]

00:02:54.132 --> 00:02:56.968
I was born in Dominican Republic,
then I came here when I was three--

00:02:57.051 --> 00:02:59.596
-Okay.
-Listen, my childhood was very different

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:01.431
than a lot of the kids
that were born here.

00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:02.724
-Okay.
-Where are you from?

00:03:02.807 --> 00:03:05.727
-Charlotte, North Carolina, honey.
-I've been there before.

00:03:06.102 --> 00:03:07.604
I went to a place called Fayetteville.

00:03:07.896 --> 00:03:09.981
-Oh, "Fayettevull."
-"Fayettevull"?

00:03:10.064 --> 00:03:13.401
-"Fayettevull," not Fayetteville.
-My accent makes me say Fayetteville.

00:03:13.484 --> 00:03:15.570
It's "Fayettevull," honey.

00:03:16.029 --> 00:03:17.405
[both laughing]

00:03:17.989 --> 00:03:19.991
So, what do you do for work?

00:03:20.074 --> 00:03:21.784
I am a real estate agent.

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:23.828
-Can you hook me up with a sweet deal?
-Absolutely.

00:03:23.912 --> 00:03:25.204
Well, I'm a firefighter.

00:03:25.496 --> 00:03:27.874
-Oh, that's awesome!
-Yeah. And a DJ.

00:03:27.957 --> 00:03:30.793
I'm actually in a band.
We play hip-hop and rock.

00:03:30.877 --> 00:03:31.920
That's cool.

00:03:32.003 --> 00:03:33.838
I work for one of my good friends.

00:03:33.922 --> 00:03:36.674
He owns a nightclub and...

00:03:36.758 --> 00:03:38.885
-Wow.
-It's a strip club.

00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:41.346
[both laugh]

00:03:41.846 --> 00:03:43.264
I'm a design technologist,

00:03:43.348 --> 00:03:46.351
which is a fancy way of saying
I'm a web designer...

00:03:46.434 --> 00:03:48.478
-Cool.
-slash user-experience designer.

00:03:48.561 --> 00:03:50.730
I could probably
chat your ear off about it, but--

00:03:50.813 --> 00:03:54.150
No, please do. I--
My job is recruiting for data scientists.

00:03:54.233 --> 00:03:56.236
-Oh, wow. Cool.
-Do you work with any robotics?

00:03:56.319 --> 00:03:59.614
No, I don't, but I think
they're really cool, super fascinating.

00:03:59.697 --> 00:04:01.491
-It's pretty wild.
-It's pretty crazy, right?

00:04:01.574 --> 00:04:03.201
-It's like Willy Wonka Factory wild.
-Yeah.

00:04:03.576 --> 00:04:04.410
Oh!

00:04:04.786 --> 00:04:06.287
[both laughing]

00:04:06.371 --> 00:04:09.832
So, what did you do to come out here,
if you don't mind me asking?

00:04:10.124 --> 00:04:13.836
Uh, when I came out here--
Um, I always wanted to move to New York.

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:14.879
Right.

00:04:14.963 --> 00:04:16.881
I've seen Rent, like, 35 times.

00:04:16.965 --> 00:04:18.091
-I love--
-Damn!

00:04:18.174 --> 00:04:20.426
Oh, well, you didn't have to react
like that!

00:04:20.510 --> 00:04:22.262
-I did. Like 35?
-I just--

00:04:23.471 --> 00:04:26.516
-That's a lot.
-I just-- [laughs] I just love New York.

00:04:26.849 --> 00:04:29.602
Then, one day, like,
I had became a flight attendant,

00:04:29.686 --> 00:04:33.481
and I'd, like, pop in for, like, 12 hours,
and then just be like, "See ya."

00:04:33.898 --> 00:04:37.193
Um, and then fly back out.
And then, I wanted to move to New York,

00:04:37.277 --> 00:04:39.821
and I wasn't really seeing
my career taking off...

00:04:40.071 --> 00:04:42.991
Pun completely intended,
being a flight attendant.

00:04:43.074 --> 00:04:44.158
-Right.
-So...

00:04:44.242 --> 00:04:45.827
Um... so, like, I moved here,

00:04:45.910 --> 00:04:48.288
and immediately moved in
with a guy I was seeing at the time,

00:04:48.371 --> 00:04:50.331
and then that ended up being

00:04:50.415 --> 00:04:51.582
-um... terrible.
-Hey.

00:04:51.666 --> 00:04:53.084
-Hello.
-Do you want to grab a drink?

00:04:53.167 --> 00:04:54.711
-Yes.
-Want to do drinks this evening?

00:04:54.794 --> 00:04:56.587
Two glasses of water to start.

00:04:56.838 --> 00:04:58.715
-Is that okay?
-Yeah. No, that's great, actually.

00:04:58.798 --> 00:05:00.508
Very responsible. I like that.

00:05:01.342 --> 00:05:03.011
I can't even pronounce that. Narra...

00:05:03.094 --> 00:05:04.637
-Wait.
-Naragans--

00:05:04.721 --> 00:05:06.806
-Let me pronounce it first.
-Okay. I'll give you your--

00:05:06.889 --> 00:05:08.474
-Then you correct me, all right?
-Okay.

00:05:09.517 --> 00:05:11.686
Narragansett?

00:05:11.769 --> 00:05:12.603
-Yes!
-Yeah?

00:05:12.687 --> 00:05:13.896
[both laughing]

00:05:14.355 --> 00:05:17.275
I just go for white wine.
Like, white wine will get me hyped up,

00:05:17.358 --> 00:05:19.402
-like two, three glasses of wine.
-Yeah! Me too.

00:05:19.485 --> 00:05:21.237
For me, whenever I go out with my girls

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:24.198
and just, like, talking shit
about everything in our lives,

00:05:24.282 --> 00:05:26.534
-we'll get--
-I'm sure you talk a lot of shit, right?

00:05:26.617 --> 00:05:27.577
[laughs]

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:30.788
-What makes you think that?
-I feel like you have a lot to say.

00:05:32.915 --> 00:05:34.125
You could say that.

00:05:34.208 --> 00:05:36.127
I'm just saying. You're not disagreeing.

00:05:36.210 --> 00:05:40.256
I'm not... I mean, I don't-- I don't--
I just-- I don't-- I don't know. Well...

00:05:40.673 --> 00:05:43.092
-I have your table ready right over here.
-Great.

00:05:43.176 --> 00:05:44.927
-Do you want to follow me?
-Awesome.

00:05:51.684 --> 00:05:52.518
[laughs]

00:05:52.602 --> 00:05:53.853
So I want to know something.

00:05:53.936 --> 00:05:55.063
Yeah, you want to know what?

00:05:55.146 --> 00:05:58.900
Tell me about your dating life here
in New York, 'cause it's crazy out here.

00:05:59.108 --> 00:06:02.320
It is. I would describe it as insane. Yes.

00:06:02.403 --> 00:06:03.363
Um...

00:06:04.155 --> 00:06:05.239
My dating life...

00:06:06.324 --> 00:06:07.200
Woof!

00:06:07.617 --> 00:06:08.743
Um...

00:06:09.035 --> 00:06:12.371
So my experience with dating apps
is, like... I'll always, like...

00:06:12.455 --> 00:06:15.666
Sometimes, you know, you go through
a period of sexual anorexia

00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:17.919
where you're like,
"I'm not gonna sleep with anybody,"

00:06:18.252 --> 00:06:19.754
and then you get tired of that.

00:06:19.837 --> 00:06:23.007
And then you're just like
left-swiping, left-swiping, left-swiping.

00:06:23.091 --> 00:06:26.135
You could find endless reasons to say no
and I think that that's so shallow.

00:06:26.469 --> 00:06:27.720
-I hate it.
-I hate the apps.

00:06:27.804 --> 00:06:29.847
I hate the apps.
I've never gotten a date from an app.

00:06:29.931 --> 00:06:32.558
-Oh, no, but you're cute.
-I'm cute. You're right, but I'm not...

00:06:32.642 --> 00:06:34.685
-Yes. So are you. You're very cute--
-Thank you.

00:06:34.769 --> 00:06:36.896
You seem to not do well
with the apps either.

00:06:36.979 --> 00:06:40.191
-I have a lot of energy. I am a handful.
-You are a high-energy person.

00:06:40.274 --> 00:06:41.234
[laughs]

00:06:43.611 --> 00:06:45.238
So, tell me about your last girlfriend.

00:06:45.321 --> 00:06:48.658
Well, I've always been attracted
to, like, older girls for some reason.

00:06:48.741 --> 00:06:51.994
-We dated for two and a half years.
-Wow.

00:06:52.829 --> 00:06:55.289
It's kind of putting me on the spot,
but she's a finance person.

00:06:55.373 --> 00:06:57.166
-Yeah, no, look. It was--
-Wow.

00:06:57.250 --> 00:06:58.709
I thought I was in love.

00:06:58.793 --> 00:07:02.755
You know, I just think that it's hard
to form a connection in New York.

00:07:02.839 --> 00:07:05.216
I kind of guess I mixed love
with, like, obsession.

00:07:05.508 --> 00:07:07.635
-Yeah
-And, like, it just didn't work out.

00:07:07.718 --> 00:07:09.387
I still have love for her.

00:07:09.470 --> 00:07:10.847
-But I'm not in love with her.
-Yes.

00:07:10.930 --> 00:07:12.348
We were together for five years.

00:07:12.974 --> 00:07:15.768
-Five years, man. That's a long time.
-That is a long time.

00:07:17.353 --> 00:07:20.148
-So, what are you thinking about?
-Um...

00:07:20.231 --> 00:07:23.025
Maybe the big salad. How are you feeling?

00:07:23.109 --> 00:07:24.861
Let's see what kind of salad they have.

00:07:24.944 --> 00:07:27.947
Um, apparently, one that is big. Big salad

00:07:28.030 --> 00:07:30.950
-of cooked and pickled raw vegetables.
-That caught your attention?

00:07:31.033 --> 00:07:32.201
-Yeah.
-You like it big?

00:07:33.870 --> 00:07:35.288
[laughs]

00:07:35.705 --> 00:07:36.956
The salad. The salad.

00:07:37.373 --> 00:07:41.002
The big salad, I wonder, if that's like
paying homage to Elaine from Seinfeld.

00:07:41.085 --> 00:07:43.254
-Don't know if you're a Seinfeld person.
-Shut up!

00:07:43.337 --> 00:07:45.715
-Yeah, I totally am.
-Yeah, the big salad.

00:07:45.798 --> 00:07:47.717
I've been known to dance
like Elaine Benes.

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:49.177
-Oh, little kicks?
-Yeah.

00:07:49.260 --> 00:07:51.262
Yeah? Oh, goodness. That's a good look.

00:07:51.345 --> 00:07:53.014
-Yeah? It's a good look? [laughs]
-Yeah.

00:07:53.097 --> 00:07:54.682
-Hopefully.
-How's it go again?

00:07:55.057 --> 00:07:56.100
It's just like...

00:07:57.018 --> 00:07:57.852
[laughs]

00:07:58.102 --> 00:07:59.645
-That's actually pretty good.
-Thank you.

00:07:59.729 --> 00:08:01.355
That's really good. I'm impressed.

00:08:01.439 --> 00:08:04.567
-It's one of my main selling points.
-Bravo. That's part of your appeal.

00:08:05.151 --> 00:08:06.819
What do you like to eat normally?

00:08:07.236 --> 00:08:08.738
I'm kind of simple. Um...

00:08:09.030 --> 00:08:11.240
-Okay.
-I've cooked at the firehouse before.

00:08:11.324 --> 00:08:12.158
Okay.

00:08:12.241 --> 00:08:13.493
-Stir-fry.
-Are you the cook or--

00:08:13.576 --> 00:08:16.120
-No, not the cook. I have cooked.
-Cooker? [laughs]

00:08:16.621 --> 00:08:18.456
When you're stressed,
you're a pressure cooker?

00:08:18.539 --> 00:08:20.917
Yeah, no. You really love puns.

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:23.127
-[laughing] I do, so much.
-You really do.

00:08:23.211 --> 00:08:24.378
It's terrible.

00:08:24.754 --> 00:08:28.007
Listen. I'm just saying, I don't know,
but you have about three more puns.

00:08:28.090 --> 00:08:30.843
I'll give you three more puns
throughout the course of the night,

00:08:30.927 --> 00:08:31.969
and that's it though.

00:08:32.053 --> 00:08:33.054
It's too many puns.

00:08:33.429 --> 00:08:36.224
I've never-- I've never encountered
so many puns in my life.

00:08:36.599 --> 00:08:38.100
Oh, my God. You're a headache.

00:08:38.351 --> 00:08:39.894
-Um...
-Sorry, honey.

00:08:39.977 --> 00:08:41.646
-But you're a cute headache.
-Thank you.

00:08:41.729 --> 00:08:43.648
So it's all right. Um...

00:08:44.732 --> 00:08:46.984
-Have a steak...
-Oh, wow. Thank you so much.

00:08:47.318 --> 00:08:48.361
With jalapeño.

00:08:48.444 --> 00:08:49.904
Yes. Do you share food?

00:08:50.321 --> 00:08:52.698
-I am a food sharer. What about you?
-Yeah, totally.

00:08:52.782 --> 00:08:54.492
-My attitude--
-We should've planned that

00:08:54.575 --> 00:08:56.410
before we both got the same thing.

00:08:57.828 --> 00:09:00.623
So we're both gonna do
these onions, right?

00:09:00.915 --> 00:09:04.210
-Definitely. Are you freaking kidding me?
-Okay. It's social suicide.

00:09:04.293 --> 00:09:06.796
I just want to make sure
that we're both on the same page here.

00:09:06.879 --> 00:09:09.048
I like to think that this is
how you find friends

00:09:09.131 --> 00:09:12.510
that care about you as a person
and not just the way that you smell.

00:09:12.843 --> 00:09:16.055
-Cheers.
-Cheers to not making new friends.

00:09:16.138 --> 00:09:17.014
[Matt] Mmm.

00:09:17.765 --> 00:09:19.350
To smelling like onions.

00:09:21.978 --> 00:09:23.479
That's nice. You got something.

00:09:23.771 --> 00:09:24.981
[mumbles indistinctly]

00:09:30.695 --> 00:09:31.821
-Well, cheers.
-Cheers.

00:09:32.280 --> 00:09:34.031
-What kind of wine is this?
-Syrah.

00:09:34.407 --> 00:09:35.992
You like Syrah? That's your style?

00:09:36.075 --> 00:09:38.327
I like Syrah, Merlot, Cabernet Sauvignon.

00:09:38.411 --> 00:09:41.122
-Mmm.
-I feel it depends on what I am eating.

00:09:41.205 --> 00:09:43.040
It needs to pair well with the meal.

00:09:43.124 --> 00:09:46.168
I haven't-- I don't have enough
of a palate for Merlot yet,

00:09:46.544 --> 00:09:48.546
-so I'm really into Pinots.
-Have you seen Sideways?

00:09:48.629 --> 00:09:51.882
-Of course. "We're not drinking Merlot!"
-"Oh, we're not drinking any Merlot!"

00:09:51.966 --> 00:09:53.509
That's the only fucking thing I know.

00:09:53.593 --> 00:09:55.803
I was gonna say,
the only thing I know about wine is--

00:09:55.886 --> 00:09:57.471
[both] Paul Giamatti--

00:09:58.097 --> 00:09:59.181
Fuck. Shut up.

00:09:59.265 --> 00:10:00.182
[laughs]

00:10:00.641 --> 00:10:02.059
-That was cute.
-That was cute.

00:10:02.143 --> 00:10:04.020
-Kind of cute.
-That was kind of cute.

00:10:04.103 --> 00:10:05.605
Just more steak.

00:10:06.564 --> 00:10:07.440
That's cute, too.

00:10:10.484 --> 00:10:11.319
[laughs]

00:10:11.902 --> 00:10:13.529
I actually sing jazz,

00:10:13.613 --> 00:10:16.824
so I love jazz as a form of expression.

00:10:16.907 --> 00:10:18.284
Yeah? Can I hear a note?

00:10:18.492 --> 00:10:19.619
Um...

00:10:20.620 --> 00:10:23.289
-Sure. Let me just--
-Right now?

00:10:23.372 --> 00:10:25.791
-You want to bite into the salad?
-Want to take a bite first?

00:10:25.875 --> 00:10:27.710
-I think I'm good.
-[laughs]

00:10:28.085 --> 00:10:30.463
Yeah, you don't want anything
in your throat, right?

00:10:31.881 --> 00:10:35.009
I guess that's a preparation,
right, before you're ready to sing,

00:10:35.092 --> 00:10:36.969
you have to have your throat clear?

00:10:39.138 --> 00:10:40.139
[laughs]

